<title>NETHERLANDS: Van Lanschot maintains KLM as outperformer.</title>
<headline>Van Lanschot maintains KLM as outperformer.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of Q3 results flash.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>KLM		 Airlines	53.90   Van Lanschot</p>
<p>COMMENT: Outperformer. Third-quarter net profit rather worse than anticipated, but KLM identifying slight improvement in market and higher dollar. Operating result seen at turning point in Q4. Traffic figures improved steadily over last seven months, and Focus 2000 seen achieving some 2/3 of its targeted 1.5 billion guilder boost to operating revenues within its set time of three years. Estimate that additional restructuring will lead to extraordinary charge of some 200-300 million guilders in Q4.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS	 P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1995/96 (actual)   5.88	 9.2     2.00</p>
<p>    1996/97		4.40	12.3     2.00</p>
<p>    1997/98		5.86	 9.2     2.00</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
